    "needs_teacher_verification": true,
    "note": "Sourced from the Sri Chaitanya Junior Fastrack zoology section, SAQ chapter 8 'Locomotion & Reproduction' (book p.40, question 37). Zoology holds only ONE source book — the TSBIE Basic Learning Material in hand covers physics only, and no zoology board paper is in the corpus — so the two-book union check and the past-paper back-test are both STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE for this card, not merely unrun; 'not checked' must never be read as 'checked and clean'. The mark split is this card's claim until a Telangana IPE teacher confirms it. APPEARANCES: the book prints [AP May-19] against the question and [AP M-16,17], [TS May-17] and [TS M-19,20] against the answer heading. BOOK WORDING CORRECTED: the book's point 9 reads 'Opisthe receives the posterior contractile vacuoles along with macro and micro nuclei', which can be read as though only the opisthe receives nuclei. BOTH daughters receive a macronucleus and a micronucleus — that is the whole point of the nuclear divisions in step 1 — and this card says so. The opisthe's own share is the POSTERIOR contractile vacuole and the new oral apparatus. The book's own timing figures are kept as printed: the fission is completed in about two hours and Paramecium may divide up to four times in a day. FIGURE SCOPE: the book prints five drawn stages; this figure draws four named stages plus labels, which is what a student can reproduce inside the time for a 4-mark answer."
  },
