    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "s1_before",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "Before the split",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Nuclei",
        "lines": [
          "Paramecium multiplies by transverse binary",
          "fission when conditions are favourable.",
          "Before the fission begins it stops feeding and",
          "the oral groove disappears.",
          "The micronucleus divides into two by mitosis.",
          "The macronucleus divides into two by amitosis."
        ],
        "why": "The cell has two kinds of nucleus and they divide in two different ways, so the marks in this step are for naming the correct division against the correct nucleus.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Swapping the two divisions. Micronucleus by mitosis, macronucleus by amitosis.",
          "Writing that fission happens in unfavourable conditions. Unfavourable conditions lead to encystment, not fission."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Micro is the small careful one and divides by mitosis; macro is the large one and divides by amitosis.",
        "margin_note": "Favourable conditions, feeding stops, then the two nuclear divisions."
      },
      {
        "id": "s2_split",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "The transverse split",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Constriction",
        "lines": [
          "A constriction then appears across the middle",
          "of the body, at right angles to the long axis.",
          "It deepens steadily until the parent is cut",
          "into two daughter individuals.",
          "The anterior daughter is called the proter and",
          "the posterior daughter is called the opisthe.",
          "The plane of division cuts across the kineties,",
          "so this fission is also called homothetogenic",
          "fission."
        ],
        "why": "The word transverse is a statement about the plane of the cut, so the answer has to say that the plane is at right angles to the long axis — that single fact separates this from the longitudinal fission of Euglena.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing or describing a lengthwise split. That is Euglena, not Paramecium.",
          "Writing proter for the posterior half. Proter is the ANTERIOR daughter."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Transverse means across, so the cut is across the slipper and the two halves are front and back.",
        "margin_note": "Name the plane, then name both daughters. The word homothetogenic is worth writing."
      },
